From 7e17b8952c77bd335a5598bd2ebeff0250778843 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koji Ishii <kojii@chromium.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:49:54 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [M156] [floats] Avoid mismatched leading floats across ruby
 columns

Original change's description:
> [floats] Avoid mismatched leading floats across ruby columns
>
> `InlineLayoutAlgorithm::PositionLeadingFloats` previously walked past
> `InlineItem::kOpenRubyColumn` (whose `IsEmptyItem()` is true) and
> positioned floats inside `<ruby>` into `LeadingFloats`. Because
> `LineBreaker::HandleRuby` lays out ruby columns in a sub-`LineBreaker`
> with empty `LeadingFloats`, those floats were laid out again without
> advancing `leading_floats_index_`, causing subsequent floats to consume
> stale `LeadingFloat` entries by index.
>
> Fix this by:
> - Stopping `PositionLeadingFloats` at `kOpenRubyColumn` and bailing when
>   resuming a ruby break token (`RubyData()`).
> - Recording each leading float's `InlineItem` index in `LeadingFloat`,
>   asserting `CHECK_EQ` on `item_index` in `LineBreaker::HandleFloat`, and
>   matching by `item_index` in `LineBreaker::RewindFloats`.
>
> Fixed: 589800513
> Change-Id: I57750a5c03b1881d368252a5340d609677da8802
